# Images and exposure. Two of them, out of one Dockerfile: the API carries no GPU
# stack, no Gyroflow and no mp4_merge, because it hands work out rather than doing it.
# Measured: 656 MB against the 1.98 GB of the single image that came before.
VS_IMAGE_API=video-stab-api:latest
VS_IMAGE_WORKER=video-stab-worker:latest
VS_PORT=8080

# Where the data lives. Must contain (or be able to create):
#   inbox/ raw/ merged/ proxies/ out/ projects/ templates/ tmp/ db/
# Keep inbox/ and raw/ on the same filesystem: ingestion then becomes an instant
# rename() instead of a multi-gigabyte copy.
VS_DATA_PATH=./data

# Owner of the files written to /data (`id -u` / `id -g`).
VS_UID=1000
VS_GID=1000

# GPU: GID of the host's `render` group (`getent group render`).
# Only used together with docker-compose.gpu.yml. It varies a lot between
# distributions (991 on Ubuntu 25.04, 105 on Debian 12, 44 or 104 elsewhere), so
# read it on the host rather than trusting this default.
VS_RENDER_GID=991

# Which GPU the host has, if any. The image carries the drivers for all of them;
# what it cannot do is choose how the GPU is handed to the container, because that
# is a Docker-level decision. So pick the matching line, and `docker compose up -d`
# applies it on its own afterwards:
#
#   nothing            no GPU, or a GPU whose stack is broken → everything on CPU
#   ...gpu.yml         AMD or Intel: maps /dev/dri, needs VS_RENDER_GID above
#   ...nvidia.yml      NVIDIA: needs nvidia-container-toolkit on the host
#
# Getting this wrong is not fatal, only slow: the application probes every
# accelerated path by actually running it and falls back to the CPU, then says so
# in the header. An `up` that forgets the override is the classic way to lose the
# GPU silently, which is what this variable exists to prevent.
#COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.gpu.yml
#COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.nvidia.yml

# auto | cuda | vaapi | cpu. `auto` probes NVDEC then VAAPI by really decoding an
# HEVC 10-bit sample, and keeps the first that works.
#
# `auto` again since 2026-08-14. VAAPI decoding was pinned off after the amdgpu
# driver deadlocked, but the real culprit was found: the machine runs AMD's
# out-of-tree amdgpu-dkms (ROCm stack, modules renamed amdttm/amdkcl/amd_sched),
# and **SIGKILLing ffmpeg while VAAPI jobs were in flight** left it waiting on a
# fence that never signalled — `Trying to push to a killed entity`, then every
# ttm_bo_delayed_delete worker stuck, reboot only. Clean decoding was never the
# problem. The worker now forwards SIGTERM to its children and compose gives it
# 60s, so that path is closed. Measured after the fix: 600 frames in 18.0s with
# VAAPI vs 28.2s on CPU, and a SIGTERM mid-decode leaves the kernel log silent.
VS_HWACCEL=auto

# Dispatcher et workers
#
# L'API est le dispatcher : elle seule ouvre la base. Un worker s'enregistre en
# HTTP, réclame un job, reçoit une spec autoportante et repose ce qu'il a mesuré.
# Il lui suffit donc de savoir où joindre l'API.
VS_API_URL=http://api:8000

# Nom du worker, et il doit être STABLE : c'est son identité, ce qui rattache ses
# mesures à sa machine. Laissé vide, le worker prend son hostname, qui ressemble à
# quelque chose de stable et n'en est pas un dans un conteneur (il change à chaque
# recréation, et laisse derrière lui une ligne `worker` orpheline).
VS_WORKER_NAME=local

# Secret partagé sur les endpoints worker. Vide = ouverts, ce qui convient tant que
# rien d'extérieur au réseau privé ne peut joindre l'API. À renseigner des deux
# côtés avant d'exposer quoi que ce soit.
VS_WORKER_TOKEN=

# --- Worker sur une autre machine (docker-compose.remote-worker.yml) --------
#
# Un worker qui ne monte pas le volume du dispatcher le découvre tout seul : l'API
# marque son `data_dir` d'un uuid, le worker envoie celui qu'il arrive à lire, et
# l'égalité est tout le test. Rien à régler, parce que le sens qui casse est
# silencieux (un worker qui croit à tort partager le volume rate tous ses jobs).
#
# Ses entrées arrivent alors en HTTP et ses sorties repartent pareil. Volume de
# travail à lui, et ce plafond dit combien de rushes il peut garder en cache : il
# supprime les plus vieux pour rester dessous. À mettre un peu sous la taille du
# volume qu'on lui donne ; 0 désactive l'éviction. Ignoré par un worker qui partage
# le volume du dispatcher, qui ne met rien en cache et n'y supprime jamais rien.
VS_WORK_PATH=./work
VS_WORKER_CACHE_BYTES=20000000000

# Ingestion (lue par l'API : c'est elle qui scanne le volume qu'elle possède)
VS_SCAN_INTERVAL_S=30
# How many consecutive scans at an identical size before a file is ingested.
VS_STABILITY_CHECKS=2
# Two parts of the same recording are contiguous within this gap (measured:
# 0.36 s on a real DJI O4 pair).
VS_SPLIT_GAP_TOLERANCE_S=2.0
# And the first part must have got close to the camera's file limit, otherwise it
# stopped because recording stopped. This is the signal that actually separates the
# two cases: measured on 179 consecutive pairs of a real O3 collection, every genuine
# split has a first part of 3.763 to 3.770 GB and follows within 0.79 s, while every
# pair the timing alone glued wrongly has a first part of 1.398 GB at most and follows
# after 1.11 s. A setting, because the limit belongs to the camera and the card.
VS_SPLIT_MIN_PART_BYTES=3000000000
# Delete the parts from raw/ after a verified merge (the merged file is lossless
# and holds everything, but the deletion cannot be undone).
VS_PURGE_PARTS_AFTER_MERGE=false

# Derush proxy
VS_PROXY_HEIGHT=960
VS_PROXY_CRF=26
